# An ordinary Python project's ignores, and the gate needs them for a reason
# (SCRUM-96): running the agreed verify leaves `__pycache__`, `*.egg-info` and
# `uv.lock` in the Worker's tree, and rite judged the workspace "not clean"
# from those — then told a step review the agent had edited outside its scope.
# It had not. rite names what it saw now, and a normal project does not leave
# these untracked in the first place.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
uv.lock
